# PIRO Feature Specification: Cytology Telepathology Evaluation Form

## Overview

Develop a new feature within the PIRO platform to support the cytology telepathology workflow. This feature will replace the current PDF-based remote cytopathologic evaluation process with an integrated web-based workflow.

The primary component will be an electronic evaluation form modeled after the PDF form currently used by the Cytology department.

The workflow is collaborative. An on-site cytology technician will initially complete the form during the procedure. The signing pathologist will later review the information, make any necessary changes, complete any remaining fields, and finalize the form.

The implementation should integrate with PIRO’s existing Angular frontend, FastAPI backend, SQL Server database, authentication system, authorization system, and user-management infrastructure.

---

# Reference Files

Use the following files located in the `temp` directory as authoritative references.

## `adequacy.pdf`

This PDF is the authoritative reference for:

- Form sections
- Field labels
- Instructions
- Static content
- Field groupings
- Repeatable specimen-site information
- General form organization

The PIRO implementation should reproduce the content and workflow represented in this PDF while following existing PIRO user-interface conventions.

## `terminologies.xlsx`

This spreadsheet contains the permitted values for categorical fields that must be implemented as drop-down controls.

Do not invent or hard-code alternative values when the applicable terminology is available in this spreadsheet.

